"guide_topic_range_title" = "Real-world range";
"guide_topic_range_body" = "WLTP figures are a standardized lab loop. Cold weather, highway speed, heater use, and headwinds all pull range down; gentle urban driving can look better than the label. Treat WLTP as an anchor, then adjust mentally for your climate and driving style.";
"guide_topic_charging_title" = "Home vs public charging";
"guide_topic_charging_body" = "Charging at home overnight is usually the cheapest kWh you will ever buy for a car. Public AC is slower but predictable; DC fast charging is convenient on trips but often priced like fuel stops, not like domestic electricity. Your mix of home vs away charging changes the monthly bill more than small differences in car efficiency.";
"guide_topic_battery_title" = "Battery longevity";
"guide_topic_battery_body" = "Modern packs are managed by software that avoids the worst stress zones most of the time. Degradation is not linear: early years see a small capacity fade, then the curve tends to flatten. Warranty floors exist for a reason, but everyday driving rarely pushes you there if thermal management and charging habits are sane.";
"guide_topic_total_cost_title" = "Total cost picture";
"guide_topic_total_cost_body" = "Sticker price is one line in a ledger that also includes energy, maintenance, insurance, depreciation, and taxes where they apply. EVs often win on energy and moving parts, while tires and insurance can surprise in either direction. The honest question is which lines dominate for your annual km and how long you keep the car.";
